<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sundgau</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sundgau is a hilly region in the south of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alsace">Alsace</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>, between Mulhouse and the Swiss border near Basel. Originally the southern of the two counties into which Alsace was divided around 740, it passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburgs</a> and belonged to Further <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> until France acquired it in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peace-of-westphalia">Peace of Westphalia</a> of 1648. Its chief town is Altkirch.</p></div>
